<title>AUSTRALIA: Regulator blocks Simsmetal Wanless buy.</title>
<headline>Regulator blocks Simsmetal Wanless buy.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Recycling group Simsmetal Ltd said on Thursday the Australian Competition and Consumer Commission (ACCC) had blocked its planned purchase of unlisted Queensland recycler, Wanless Metal Industries Ltd.</p>
<p>The ACCC said in its view the proposal would have substantially lessened competition in the Queensland metals recycling market.</p>
<p>In a statement, Simsetal said it disagreed with the ACCC's view and would review its position with its legal advisers.</p>
<p>The ACCC decision leaves the way open for Metalcorp Ltd to acquire the Wanless assets.  </p>
<p>Metalcorp made an offer for Wanless on March 25 but Simsetal had a right of first refusal.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
